Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:38:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vmm: a vCPU thread is the host's to prepare when it is made

start_threaded calls vmm::ext::vcpu_thread::spawned with the new thread's
handle, on the thread that makes it, while the microVM is still being
built. Nothing on Linux. On macOS the vCPU thread is given the latency
tier a guest's timer waits need; the call it takes is denied once the
sandbox has narrowed, so it cannot be made later from the thread itself.
A refusal fails the start as a failed spawn does.
---
 src/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs b/src/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs
index 5af0b76dc6b0891b6a6ea4de282f32eb97094d65..e967026be3c95678f2c4fbca5b0714867cf825ba 100644
--- a/src/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs
+++ b/src/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs
@@ -200,6 +200,9 @@ impl Vcpu {
                 self.run(filter);
             })
             .map_err(StartThreadedError::Spawn)?;
+        // wick: what the host does to a vCPU thread when it is made
+        // (vmm::ext::vcpu_thread).
+        crate::ext::vcpu_thread::spawned(&vcpu_thread).map_err(StartThreadedError::Spawn)?;
 
         Ok(VcpuHandle::new(
             event_sender,
